<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="227b" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>H8 grants the customer's BFF identities access to the "Spaarke Model 1" container type (plan G9)</title>
    <phase>Model 1 dedicated-stamp remediation — plan §7 T227 (gap G9)</phase>
    <gate>after 227a</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>L2 handler code (.cs) calling Graph as the SPE owning app; auth-adjacent; tests.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>One idempotent GET-then-PUT step in an existing handler, reusing the T248 owning-app client.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <tags>provisioning, provisioning-handler, l2-controlplane, spe, auth, model1-dedicated, testing</tags>
    <deps>227a</deps>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Before H8 creates the customer's container, grant the stamp UAMI and the customer's BFF app registration access to the Spaarke Model 1 container type.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer (L2 control plane, Microsoft Graph SPE APIs). Follow the provisioning and auth constraints.</role>

  <goal>
    H8 ensures two applicationPermissionGrants on the container-type registration — the stamp UAMI (InterStepState.MiClientId,
    application full) and the BFF app registration (InterStepState.BffAppRegId, delegated full) — as the owning app,
    idempotently, before creating the container.
  </goal>

  <justification>
    <existing>H8SpeContainerHandler (owning-app Graph client via SpeConfidentialClientGraphFactory + SpeContainerOptions.TryGetOwner); SpeOwnerCredentialProbe (registration GET); scripts/Register-BffMiWithContainerType.ps1 (same PUT, beta, certificate).</existing>
    <extension>Add a grant step inside H8 — it already holds the owning-app client, owner lookup and container type id, and runs after H3 and H2a. No new handler or DAG node.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The customer BFF's SPE calls (OBO as the BFF app; app-only as the UAMI) get 403: no handler grants either identity on the container type, so every document operation on a new stamp fails.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <context>
    <background>
      Microsoft Learn (v1.0): PUT /storage/fileStorage/containerTypeRegistrations/{containerTypeId}/applicationPermissionGrants/{appId}
      body { delegatedPermissions: [..], applicationPermissions: [..] } → 201; app permission FileStorageContainerTypeReg.Selected
      (changes limited to registrations owned by the calling app); grants may take up to one hour to propagate. The owning app's
      MI-FIC token (T248) carries FileStorageContainerTypeReg.Selected (live probe 2026-10-03). Topology doc :287-292: a grant for
      the app registration does not cover the UAMI. H10 separately gives the UAMI Graph app role FileStorageContainer.Selected.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/SpeContainer/H8SpeContainerHandler.cs (+ GraphContainerProvisioner.cs, SpeConfidentialClientGraphFactory.cs)</file>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/Preflight/SpeOwnerCredentialProbe.cs (registration GET pattern)</file>
      <file>H13 acceptance probes (grant verification)</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/SPAARKE-SPE-CONTAINER-TYPE-TOPOLOGY.md §3A/§5; SPAARKE-ENVIRONMENT-RESOURCE-INVENTORY.md container-type registration row; SPAARKE-SPE-TOPOLOGY-SETUP-RUNBOOK.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/provisioning.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <decisions>
    <decision date="2026-10-06" by="agent, from evidence">The grant step lives in H8 (not a new handler): H8 already owns the owning-app client and runs after H3 + H2a.</decision>
    <decision date="2026-10-06" by="agent, from evidence">Each identity gets only the token kind it presents (GraphClientFactory: app-only Graph = the UAMI when Graph:ManagedIdentity:Enabled; OBO = the BFF app): UAMI application [full], delegated [none]; BFF app delegated [full], application [none]. Trimming below full needs a BFF call-site audit — out of scope.</decision>
    <decision date="2026-10-06" by="agent, from evidence">No H13 grant re-check (POML step 2 / third criterion dropped): H8's GET-then-PUT/PATCH confirms each grant from Graph's own response and re-checks on every re-run; nothing removes a grant between H8 and H13. H8 does not wait for the up-to-1h propagation.</decision>
    <decision date="2026-10-06" by="owner (D28)">One container type per model, one container per customer (per Dataverse environment). App-only grants reach every container of the shared type (Microsoft: no per-container app scoping) — isolation for app-only SPE calls is enforced in code with tests (T227d). A container type per customer was rejected.</decision>
  </decisions>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="idempotent">GET the grant first; PUT only when missing or different. Failure → Resumable with a code naming the app id; never Quarantine for a Graph 5xx/429.</constraint>
    <constraint source="I5">Token is per-tenant (explicit tenant id); no ambient credential.</constraint>
    <constraint source="tests">Tests use the existing H8 test transport (no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; per ADR-038); cover: both PUTs sent with the right bodies as the owning app; second run sends no PUT; missing BffAppRegId / MiClientId → fail before any Graph call; 403 → Resumable.</constraint>
    <constraint source="scope">No live Graph change in this task.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">H8: grant step (GET-then-PUT for both identities) before container create; inputs declared in HandlerRunInputs if new.</step>
    <step order="2">H13: verify both grants (GET) — extend the existing SPE acceptance probe.</step>
    <step order="3">Tests; docs (topology §3A/§5, inventory row, runbook).</step>
    <step order="4">Verify (ControlPlane.Tests, Worker build, ArchTests); Step 9.5; close.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">H8 test: a run sends PUT applicationPermissionGrants/{MiClientId} and /{BffAppRegId} with the stated bodies before the container POST; a re-run sends no PUT.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">H8 test: missing BffAppRegId or MiClientId fails before any Graph request; a 403 on the PUT is Resumable.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Graph-level test (real SDK): a missing grant is PUT without appId in the body; a matching grant writes nothing; a different one is PATCHed; a refused GET/write fails naming the app.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ControlPlane.Tests, Worker build and ArchTests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    COMPLETED 2026-10-06 (FULL).
    - ISpeContainerProvisioner.EnsureGrantsAsync (seam extended, no new interface); GraphContainerProvisioner: GET grant ->
      404 -> PUT (Learn's create; SDK 6.5.0 has no typed PUT, so the PATCH request info is sent with HttpMethod PUT via the
      request adapter, ODataError mapping) | different -> PATCH | same -> nothing. Empty sets are sent as ["none"] (what GET
      reports). An update logs the previous permissions.
    - H8 step 5b after the idempotency no-op and before container creation; rejection codes spe-grant-identity-missing,
      spe-container-type-grant-failed, spe-container-type-grant-infra-fault (all Resumable). BuildGrants(uami, bffApp).
    - HandlerRunInputs H8 += MiClientId, BffAppRegId; DagAdvancer comment: H3 is a data edge again.
    - Tests: H8 AC-18..AC-20 (order, request, missing ids, refused / faulted grant, AC-9 no grant call when complete);
      GraphContainerProvisionerGrantTests G1-G4 (real SDK, scripted HttpMessageHandler).
    - Docs: topology §3A (H8 owns grants; D28 app-only caveat), runbook Step 9 (sample body, H8), inventory row, Worker comment,
      provisioning constraints (D28 rule), design.md decision, plan D28 / G9 / G32.
    - Verification: ControlPlane.Tests 2120/0/1, Worker build 0 warnings, ArchTests 363/363.
    - Step 9.5: code-review CRITICAL (app-only grant on the shared type reaches every customer's container) -> researcher
